Docker Network Setup: Beta on Application Server 2
This repository documents the automation and execution steps for setting up a custom Docker bridge network on Application Server 2 (stapp02) as part of the Nautilus DevOps infrastructure requirements.

Task Overview
The goal was to create a dedicated Docker network named beta on stapp02 configured with a bridge driver, a specific subnet, and an isolated IP range.

Requirements
Target Server: Application Server 2 (stapp02)

Network Name: beta

Driver: bridge

Subnet: 172.28.0.0/24

IP Range: 172.28.0.0/24

Execution Guide
1. Connect to Application Server 2
Access the server via the jump host using the provided credentials:

Bash
ssh steve@stapp02
(Password: Am3ric@)

2. Create the Docker Network
Execute the Docker command to spin up the network with the required specifications:

Bash
docker network create \
  --driver bridge \
  --subnet 172.28.0.0/24 \
  --ip-range 172.28.0.0/24 \
  beta
3. Verify Configuration
Inspect the newly created network to ensure properties are correctly applied:

Bash
docker network inspect beta
